
--
-- Every case opens with `press a`, because every game opens on its title
-- screen. That is one line of ceremony in exchange for the title screen
-- being part of what the suite checks rather than something it routes
-- around: a game that never reached `play` would fail every case below.
test the wall starts whole
press a
expect left.value = 8
expect score.value = 0

test the ball breaks a brick and the brick stops being solid
press a
play 240 ticks
expect score.value >= 1
expect left.value <= 7

test the bat runs to the left wall and stops
press a
hold left for 300 ticks
expect bat.x = 0
expect bat.xdirection = 0

test the bat runs to the right wall and stops
press a
hold right for 300 ticks
expect bat.right = screenwidth
expect bat.xdirection = 0

test losing the ball re-serves rather than ending the game
press a
play 600 ticks
expect scene play
expect ball1.y > 0
